      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T22:05:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point, thanks. Done in the new patch set, to match `p3s_swapin_map_sibling_slices()`:\n- only the faulting PTE is made young and dirty, as in `wp_page_copy()`;\n- each sibling keeps the young, dirty and soft-dirty bits of the PTE it replaces, taken from what `ptep_clear_flush()` returns;\n- a sibling gets `maybe_mkwrite()` only when `!pte_needs_soft_dirty_wp()`.\n\nOn arm64 `pte_sw_mkyoung()` is a no-op and `vm_page_prot` already sets `PTE_AF`, so an old sibling gets an explicit `pte_mkold()`. uffd-wp needs no handling here, since `p3s_wp_slice_bounds()` skips userfaultfd-armed VMAs. The sibling case is in a small `p3s_wp_mk_sibling_pte()` helper next to `p3s_wp_install_folio_slices()`.",
